---
title: Baked Beans
author: Mildred McKinzie
category: Veggies
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@dry navy beans{3%c}
@chopped onion{1%medium}
@brown sugar{1%c}
@molasses{2%Tbsp}
@salt pork{1/4%lb} (diced)
@ketchup{1%c}
@dry mustard{2%tsp}
@salt{1%Tbsp}
@water{1%c}

Soak dry navy beans overnight or all day, then cook for 1 hour or until tender. Place the beans (not liquid) in slow cooker.

Add: @chopped onion{1%medium}, @brown sugar{1%c}, @molasses{2%Tbsp}, @salt pork{1/4%lb}, @ketchup{1%c}, @dry mustard{2%tsp}, @salt{1%Tbsp}, and @water{1%c}.

Mix well and cook 10-12 hours on low in slow cooker.
